From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: fill DrawIconEx's whole flicker-free background

Purpose: XP's Static draws the Run dialog's icon stretched to 32x33 with the
dialog's brush; Wine left the 33rd row black.
Windows behavior: with hbrFlickerFreeDraw, the offscreen bitmap of cxWidth
by cyWidth is first filled with the brush.
Wine before: filled width by width (an upstream Wine 11.0 bug).
Change: fill width by height.
Scope: all processes.
---
 dlls/win32u/cursoricon.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/cursoricon.c b/dlls/win32u/cursoricon.c
index 217ac59..e8f3bda 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/cursoricon.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/cursoricon.c
@@ -882,7 +882,7 @@ BOOL WINAPI NtUserDrawIconEx( HDC hdc, INT x0, INT y0, HICON icon, INT width,
         HBRUSH prev_brush;
         RECT r;
 
-        SetRect(&r, 0, 0, width, width);
+        SetRect(&r, 0, 0, width, height);
 
         if (!(hdc_dest = NtGdiCreateCompatibleDC(hdc))) goto failed;
         if (!(offscreen_bitmap = NtGdiCreateCompatibleBitmap(hdc, width, height)))
